        }
      ],
      "impact": "The Ethernet LEDs (D14, D23) and the activity LED (D4) will never light up because their anodes are floating.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["SW6", "R34", "R35"],
      "pins": ["SW6.1", "SW6.2", "SW6.3", "SW6.4", "R34.2", "R35.2"],
      "nets": ["Net-(R34-Pad2)", "Net-(R35-Pad2)", "/CAN0_P", "/CAN1_P"],
      "observed": "SW6 is a 2x SPST DIP switch. Switch 1 (pins 1-2) connects R34.2 to R35.2. Switch 2 (pins 3-4) connects /CAN1_P to /CAN0_P. R34.1 is on /CAN0_N, R35.1 is on /CAN1_N.",
      "expected": "R34 should connect between /CAN0_N and /CAN0_P via one switch; R35 should connect between /CAN1_N and /CAN1_P via the other switch. The two CAN buses should remain separate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(R34-Pad2) : R34.2(passive) SW6.1(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(R35-Pad2) : R35.2(2,passive) SW6.2(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/CAN0_P : ... SW6.4(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/CAN1_P : ... SW6.3(passive)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Closing the DIP switches will short CAN0_P to CAN1_P and connect the two termination resistors between CAN0_N and CAN1_N, bridging the two isolated CAN buses and causing bus contention.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R28"],
      "pins": ["R28.1", "R28.2"],
      "nets": ["+3V3", "SCL0_GPIO45"],
      "observed": "R28 has value \"10\" but its MPN is 0603WAF1002T5E, which is a 10kΩ resistor. It is used as a pull-up on SCL0_GPIO45.",
      "expected": "R28 should be 10kΩ to match the MPN and the companion pull-up R23 (10K) on SDA0_GPIO44.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "R28 | 10 | Resistor_SMD:R_0603_1608Metric | MotorController:TAYLOR_RESISTOR |  | LCSC=C25804, MPN= 0603WAF1002T5E, Manufacturer=UNI-ROYAL(Uniroyal Elec)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "R23 | 10K | Resistor_SMD:R_0603_1608Metric | MotorController:TAYLOR_RESISTOR |  | LCSC=C25804, MPN= 0603WAF1002T5E, Manufacturer=UNI-ROYAL(Uniroyal Elec)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "A 10Ω pull-up on the I2C SCL line will heavily load the bus, likely preventing I2C communication and potentially damaging the drivers.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple anomalies: a floating LED power net, cross-connected CAN termination switches, and an incorrect I2C pull-up value. These would cause non-functional status LEDs, bridged CAN buses, and I2C communication failure."
}

